    <briefdescription>
<para>Growth model for resource-type species. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="class_resource_species_growth" kindref="compound">ResourceSpeciesGrowth</ref> represents the growth properties of a resource species. It extends the general <ref refid="class_species_growth" kindref="compound">SpeciesGrowth</ref> class with additional ecological parameters relevant only to resources, such as:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>fixed wet biomass per cell,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>minimum and maximum relative humidity (RH) thresholds that determine whether the resource can grow.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The class may be constructed from a JSON configuration, enabling flexible species definitions. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
